The High Sorcerer is the elite class of the Sorcerer (neutral wizard route).
It asks no alignment at level 30. It is the wizard's burst class: one Arcane
Lance, thrown harder, sooner and twice, from a chant that blows rarely break.
It keeps every rank of the Sorcerer (<ansi fg="command">help wizard-routes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 High Lance        the Lance deals 40% more damage in all
  35 Gathered chant    the Lance chants a round less
  40 Unbroken chant    blows break its chant 50% less often in all
  45 Twin Lance        the Lance also strikes a second foe for half its damage
  50 Efficient lance   the Lance costs 12
  55 Bottomless well    +20% maximum mana
  60 Instant Lance     once a battle, its first Lance needs no chant

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it plays</ansi>

Everything is automatic. A Sorcerer casts as any wizard does (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>),
but it looses an Arcane Lance whenever it has the mana, and Magic Missile only
when it has not. The Lance chants longest of any wizard spell (3 rounds, 2
once it gathers its chant), so a Sorcerer is best shielded in the back row. The
Instant Lance says so: (instant lance, no chant), and the Twin Lance's second
bolt reads "A second lance of light strikes".

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Wizard elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves, Focused Will, Spell
Edge. See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help wizard-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>.
